Certainly! Here's an example of an X++ script to create a custom REST service in Dynamics AX:

```x++
[HttpService(HttpVerb::Get, 'api/customservice/getdata')]
public class CustomService
{
    public void getdata()
    {
        RestServiceResult result = new RestServiceResult();

        // Retrieve the required data
        MyData data = this.getMyData();

        // Prepare the response
        result.Content = JsonConverter::toJson(data);
        result.ContentType = HttpContentType::Json;
        result.StatusCode = HttpStatusCode::OK;

        // Return the response
        this.setResult(result);
    }

    private MyData getMyData()
    {
        // Implement the logic to retrieve the required data
        MyData data = new MyData();
        data.Name = "John Doe";
        data.Age = 30;
        data.Email = "john.doe@example.com";

        return data;
    }
}

[DataContract]
public class MyData
{
    [DataMember]
    public String Name;

    [DataMember]
    public int Age;

    [DataMember]
    public String Email;
}
```

In this example, we're creating a custom REST service class called `CustomService`. The `[HttpService]` attribute is used to define the HTTP verb (GET in this case) and the URL path for the service. The `getdata()` method is the entry point for the service, where you can implement the logic to retrieve and return the required data.

Inside the `getdata()` method, we're creating a `RestServiceResult` object to prepare the response. We're setting the content of the response to a JSON representation of the `MyData` object, which is returned by the `getMyData()` method. We're also setting the content type and the HTTP status code.

Finally, we're calling the `setResult()` method to return the response to the client.

The `MyData` class is a simple data contract class that represents the data structure you want to return from the service.

To use this custom REST service, you can call the URL `api/customservice/getdata` using an HTTP GET request. The service will respond with a JSON representation of the `MyData` object.

You can further customize this script to handle different HTTP verbs, accept request parameters, and perform more complex data operations as per your requirements.

